ironmental Health & Safety Exercise Science & Athletic Training Facilities Finance Finance and Administration Finance and Analytics Financial Aid Frederick Douglass Institute Geography Geology & Environment Global and Community Engagement Graduate Admissions Grants & Sponsored Research Health Services Health and Rehabilitation Sciences Healthcare and Administration Heating Plant History Homeland/Corporate Security & Leadership Honors Program Hospitality, Event Management and Tourism Housing and Residence Life Human Resources Human Resources and Compliance ID Card Office Inclusive Excellence Interdisciplinary Programs Languages, Literatures, Cultures, and Writing Leadership Development Library Macoskey Center Mailing Services Management Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics Military Science (ROTC) Modern Languages & Cultures Music Networking Nursing Office of the Provost Orientation Parking Parks and Conservation Program Payroll Philanthropy, Non-Profit Leadership & Public Affairs Philanthropy, Nonprofit Leadership & Public Affairs Philosophy Physical & Health Education Physician Assistant Program Physician Assistant Studies Police Political Science President's Office Printing Services Provost Office - 2 Psychology Public Health Public Relations Purchasing Recreational Therapy Residence Life Retention Services Robert M. Smith Student Center Safety Management School of Business School of Physical Therapy Secondary Ed & Foundation Social Sciences Social Work Special Education Sport Management, Hospitality & Tourism Sports Promotion & Information Stone House Center for Public Humanities Storm Harbor Equestrian Center Strategic Communications and Media Student Accounts Student Affairs Student Center & Conference Services Student Conduct Student Engagement and Leadership Student Health & Wellness Student Services Student Support Technology Support Services Theatre Undergraduate Admissions University Advancement University Marketing and Communication Women's Center Zone 1 Zone 2 Zone 3 Zone 4 Position Type No Selection Non-Instructional Instructional Classification Title (12) To view the position details and/or apply to an open position, click on the position title or the View Details link.  If you would like to bookmark a position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email a position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. Position Type Department Posting Number Employee Group Classification Title Mechanical Engineering | Assistant Professor Tenure Track Spring 2027| I02574 Instructional Engineering I02574 Faculty Assistant Professor SRU invites applications for one full-time tenure-track assistant professor position in mechanical engineering starting spring semester 2027. This position will be responsible for teaching undergraduate courses from fundamental engineering courses to upper division Mechanical engineering courses including instruction in engineering software packages such as CAD, CAM, MATLAB, Python, and Labview... View Details Bookmark Patrol Officer | N01234 Non-Instructional Police N01234 Staff Patrol Officer Slippery Rock University is currently recruiting for a patrol officer. Patrol officers on a university campus perform community oriented policing. Our officers are highly interactive with the student population as many students are away from home for the first time and seek guidance and direction from our officers. The role is one of assistance and enforcement, and the officers are viewed as pr... View Details Bookmark Maintenance Repairman 1 Non-Instructional Facilities N01225 Staff Maintenance Repairman 1 MAINTENANCE REPAIRMAN 1DEFINITION: This is semi-skilled maintenance and repair work in the building, mechanical or electrical trades.An employee in this class works in a variety of trades at the sub-journey level in the maintenance and repair of public buildings and equipment. Work involves minor repair jobs of a routine nature, which are carried out with only general supervision, or more advan... View Details Bookmark Semi-Skilled Laborer - 3 positions Non-Instructional Campus Grounds & Services N01231 Staff Semi-Skilled Laborer Mowing turf with rotary push and riding mowers, string trimmersTree trimming and removal using chainsaws and hand trimming equipmentGeneral landscaping including: tree, flower and shrub planting, seeding and mulchingPatching potholes and repairs to roadsSnow removalTrash pick upUse of pickup trucks, dump trucks, box trucks, cargo vans, golf carts, utility carts, street sweeper and other various... View Details Bookmark Security Officer 1 | Dispatcher | N01230 Non-Instructional Police N01230 Staff Security Officer 1 | Dispatcher Dispatching for police officers of Slippery Rock University Police Department.Answering phone calls, radio calls, and traffic control to assist in directing and parking vehicles and patrol services.Slippery Rock University provides a comprehensive package of employer benefits to eligible employees and their enrolled dependent(s), which include*:Medical, prescription drug, and supplemental benef... View Details Bookmark SUA 2 | Assistant Director, Student Support Non-Instructional Student Support N01222 Staff SUA 2 As the Assistant Director of Student Support this position reports to the Dean of Students and works to coordinate services designed to increase student retention and success by directly focusing on support for students experiencing a variety of challenging life circumstances. The Assistant Director manages a caseload of students, provides follow-up services, and provides training and education... View Details Bookmark Web Specialist and WordPress Manager Non-Instructional University Marketing and Communication N01226 Manager Manager 170 The Web Specialist and WordPress Manager will lead management and continuous improvement of the university web properties to drive enrollment, engagement, and alumni relations; serve as the primary WordPress owner, sru.edu content governance lead, and accessibility steward for all public-facing web properties; and collaborate with marketing, academic units, enrollment, IT, and campus partners t... View Details Bookmark SUA 2 | Assistant Director of Admissions for International Recruitment Non-Instructional Undergraduate Admissions N01216 Professional SUA 2 Works with the VP for Enrollment Management to carry out the following responsibilities:● Coordinate and facilitate the international admissions process, working directly with relevant staff and student applicants to ensure efficient and timely processing of international undergraduate, post-baccalaureate, transfer, and graduate applications.● Make admissions decisions on international undergra... View Details Bookmark HVAC Refrigeration Maintenance Mechanic | N01211 Non-Instructional Zone 2 N01211 Staff HVAC Refrigeration Maintenance Mechanic An employee in this role performs routine maintenance, inspections, and repairs on HVAC and refrigeration system components. Work involves responding to corrective maintenance work order requests, troubleshooting, and performing adjustments to equipment to resolve equipment deficencies. Work performed ncludes inspecting, replacing(cleaning) faulty or worn parts, such as compressors, condensers,... View Details Bookmark Special Education Instructor  | Temporary  (1.0 FTE ) 2026-2027| I02521 Instructional Special Education I02521 Faculty Instructor Online and face to face teaching and supervision of student teachers during school hours at the placement site. View Details Bookmark Chemistry Instructor | Part-Time Temporary | Fall 2026| I02491 Instructional Chemistry and Environmental Geosciences I02491 Faculty Instructor The candidate is expected to teach 2 sections of General Chemistry I lab or Organic Chemistry I lab and hold office hours during the fall 2026 semester. View Details Bookmark Electrician | multiple positions N01169 Non-Instructional Zone 1 N01169 Staff Electrician This is skilled work in the installation, troubleshooting, repair, replacement, and maintenance of electrical systems, components, and equipment that operate with up to 480 volts of electricity.Locates, troubleshoots, and resolves power failures and circuitry issues; and installs and commissions a variety of electrical systems, components, equipment, and fixtures.Tests equipment and connections... View Details Bookmark ADMISSIONS Undergraduate Graduate International Financial Aid/Costs Orientation Visit ACADEMICS Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Academic Departments Colleges Library Academic Services CAMPUS LIFE Living on campus Dining Bookstore Wellness Volunteering Get Involved SPORTS Intercollegiate Athletics Intramural Sports Club Sports Recreation Center Sports Information Rock Athletic Club ABOUT SRU University Profile Accountability Extended Learning Community Employment Arts and Culture NEWS & INFO News Releases Events, Tickets, Calendars Directories Campus Map top of the rock rockpride online Copyright Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania • 1 Morrow Way Slippery Rock, PA 16057 • Webmaster • Right to Know Policy • Sitemap • Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
