      "title": "Slippery Rock University | Special Education Instructor  | Temporary  (1.0 FTE ) 2026-2027| I02521",
      "description": "Slippery Rock University | Special Education Instructor  | Temporary  (1.0 FTE ) 2026-2027| I02521 Skip to Main Content STUDENTS FACULTY AND STAFF ADMINISTRATION ALUMNI, FRIENDS, GIVING PARENTS ADMISSIONS ACADEMICS CAMPUS LIFE ATHLETICS ABOUT SRU NEWS and INFO Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About SRU Human Resources Diversity and Equal Opportunity Benefits Directions Visitors and Community Special Education Instructor  | Temporary  (1.0 FTE ) 2026-2027| I02521 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Official graduate and undergraduate transcripts are required for this position. If official transcripts are not on file with the university, please upload them using the online system or submit them to: Office of Human Resources 205 Old Main Slippery Rock University Slippery Rock, PA 16057. Official transcripts are required prior to appointment. Recommended candidates will be required to complete criminal background check, including Act 34 Background Check and Act 151 (Child Abuse) Background Check and Federal Criminal (FBI) clearance prior to appointment. The recommended candidate will also be required to submit a completed Act 24 form (PDE-6004) prior to employment Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Details Posting Number I02521 Classification Title Instructor Working Title Special Education Instructor  | Temporary  (1.0 FTE ) 2026-2027| I02521 Employee Group Faculty Bargaining Unit APSCUF Location Main Campus Department Special Education Pay Rate Employment Type Temporary FT Work Schedule The proposed course schedule will require face to face on campus teaching of students throughout the day between 8:00 AM and 4:30 PM. The position also requires travel to supervise field students or student teaching at the field placement site. Position Summary Information Position Summary Online and face to face teaching and supervision of student teachers during school hours at the placement site. Minimum Qualifications Three years successful teaching in public schools. Masters degree in special education or related field. Commitment to the education of diverse populations. Successful performance in an interview including a teaching demonstration. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in Higher Education, Experienced supervising field and student teachers. Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Respect for Individuals in the Community Slippery Rock University provides an environment that respects, encourages, and promotes the talents and contributions of all. Slippery Rock University values a community with a shared sense of purpose, where people demonstrate mutual respect and appreciation. Slippery Rock University values diversity that honors and includes all persons regardless of age, creed, disability, ethnic heritage, gender, gender identity, race, religion, sexual orientation, or socioeconomic status in academic and extracurricular endeavor, in the working environment, and in the daily life of the university community. Notice of Non-Discrimination Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, religion, age, disability, or veteran status in its programs or activities in accordance with Title IX of the Educati